[E-REFL] Error: `rfl` can't prove this
    ╭─[ reject/rfl-long-computed.sw:18:75 ]
    │
 18 │ theorem wrongRepeated (r: Range) (k: Nat) (n: Nat): r.repeated k n = 0 := rfl
    │                                                                           ─┬─  
    │                                                                            ╰─── `r.repeated k n` and `0` aren't equal
    │ 
    │ Note 1: computing the left side gives `if (List.rangeFrom n 0).foldLeft 0 (acc x => acc + …) ≠ 0 then if (if … <= … then … / … else Nat.pow 10 …) ≤ (if … <= … then … - 1 else … / …) then (List.rangeFrom n 0).foldLeft 0 (acc x => …) * (… * … / 2) else 0 else 0`
    │ 
    │ Note 2: `rfl` proves `a = b` only when both sides compute to the same value
    │ 
    │ Note 3: this statement is false; a counterexample:
    │           r = { lo = 0, hi = 1 }
    │           k = 1
    │           n = 1
    │         `r.repeated k n = 0` is false:
    │           left:  1
    │           right: 0
